url: "https://github.com/spectralbranding/orgschema-papers"
abstract: >
  Hub repository indexing the Organizational Schema Theory (OST) research corpus.
  OST is a reverse-design test-driven methodology for business operations in which
  organizations are specified backward from desired customer experience through a
  six-tier cascade of testable, version-controlled specifications. Each paper-slug
  subdirectory contains a peer-reviewed working paper, supporting computation, and
  per-paper reproduction artifacts (CITATION.cff, reproduce.sh, output/). The hub
  itself provides the cross-paper index, the dual-licence framing, and the
  orchestrator that iterates per-paper reproduction pipelines.
keywords:
  - "organizational schema theory"
  - "six-tier ontology"
  - "specification readiness"
  - "test-driven business design"
  - "verification as operator"
  - "spectral brand theory"
